# Valgrind suppressions for tools/test-valgrind.sh. Each one names the exact
# frames it hides and why the report is not a defect.

# std 0.16 lib/std/compress/flate/Compress.zig, huffman.buildValues: for every
# symbol it reads base[bits]. A symbol with bit length 0 has frequency 0 and
# base[0] is never set, so its code is undefined; such a symbol is never
# written. std says so there: "For `b == 0` this is fine since v is specified
# to be undefined." zpdf's tests inflate every compressed stream and compare it
# with the uncompressed one, which would fail if an undefined code were used.
{
   std-flate-huffman-code-of-unused-symbol
   Memcheck:Cond
   fun:*huffman.buildValues
   fun:*huffman.build
}
